231:
The county has established the Lumpkin County Drug Abuse Treatment and Education Fund Advisory Committee to oversee the drug abuse treatment and education fund. The purpose of the committee is to review and approve all requests for funding and expenditures from the drug abuse treatment and education fund as delegated by the county board. The committee shall consist of the following members:
(1) One representative appointed by the county board;
(2) One representative nominated by the chief judge of the county superior court and appointed by the county board;
(3) One representative nominated by the judge of the county juvenile court and appointed by the county board;
(4) One representative nominated by the chief judge of the county magistrate court and appointed by the county board;
(5) One representative nominated by the judge of the county probate court and appointed by the county board;
(6) One representative nominated by the county sheriff and appointed by the county board;
(7) One representative nominated by the county district attorney and appointed by the county board;
(8) The person serving as the clerk of the superior court; provided, however, that this appointee shall serve as a nonvoting member of the committee; and
(9) The person serving as the chief county probation officer; provided, however, that this appointee shall serve as a nonvoting member of the committee.
(Res. No. 2009-61, § 2(A)—(G), 9-11-2009)
